    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0453" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Brigadier General Henry A.
                            Byroade to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-24">24 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>495. Field Team 8 states that National Govt headquarters at Canton has not
                    received formal recognition of the Communist forces in the Canton area. Team
                    states that without this recognition it cannot implement cease-fire order on
                    Tapeng Peninsula. Your 186<anchor n="47" xml:id="d202-f1"/> states that Gimo has
                    issued orders to General Chang Fa Kwei to allow Ex Hq team to proceed to
                    disputed area but was not specific on recognition of East River column. Please
                    furnish results of any action taken on our 357.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d202-f2"
                    /></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
